69 more authors hold 13.7% together. The largest of them is Alec Thomas at 1.0%.

**Concentration:**
- **Bus factor:** it is 5, meaning the smallest number of authors whose surviving lines reach 50% of the lines counted. Eric Paris, Noah Dietz, Alex Ogier and two more together hold 51.0%. Reaching 80% takes 16 authors. Both figures cover all Go files in the repo.
- **No single point of failure:** the top person holds 16.8%. Losing the top two removes about 27%.
- **Activity:** the five people with 50% have not committed since 2015–2018. Active contributors (2025–2026) are Georges Varouchas (3.6%), Ethan P., Maximilian Frank, Lena Voss and Hu Jun, with about 9.8% of the lines between them. Surviving lines do not show who still understands the code, so for review you will mostly rely on people who own little of it.
- **Commits vs lines:** Noah Dietz has 10.2% of the lines from 2 commits. Albert Nigmatzianov is the opposite, with 10.6% of the commits but 1.7% of the lines.

**What was left out or adjusted:**
- **Dropped files:** 3 files and 1,576 lines are not in any number. They are vendored code (2 files, 1,088 lines) and the generated `zz_generated_flags.go` (488 lines).
- **Bots:** `dependabot[bot]` is excluded and has 0 surviving lines.
- **Same-address identities:** three people appear under two names with one email, and the table counts each as one person. They are Mitch Connors / therealmitchconnors, Albert Nigmatzianov / bogem, and Charlie R.C / xilabao. This comes from names and addresses, so it is a guess. I did not write a `.mailmap`.
- **Mechanical rewrites:** I checked for them and set none aside automatically. Three commits look mechanical and were kept in the table:
  - `6bf5b04`, the `interface{}` to `any` rewrite by Sam Okafor, touched 39 files with 49 lines changed.
  - `d16d05e` by bogem, 28 lines.
  - `92abf19` by bogem, 1 line.

  I re-ran with `6bf5b04` ignored. Those 49 lines went back to earlier authors, for example Eric Paris moves to 1,802 (17.0%). The bus factor stays 5, and reaching 80% drops to 15.
- **Copy detection:** it moved 519 lines in 16 files to other authors. With copy detection Alex Ogier has 1,074 lines (10.1%) and without it 749 (7.1%). Riobard has 405 (3.8%) with it and 722 (6.8%) without.

**Limits:** these numbers show whose lines survive, not code quality, review work, design discussions or deleted code.
